magick, rather than being born. I got this idea from a M: Revised Merit. She got a few extra Attribute dots and things like that.<br /> <br /> Setting is 1955 America. PCs can come from anywhere; they just have to be resident in Hanover, NH at game start.<br /> <br /> Her concept an English noble lady (Lola) whose father fell in love with and married a beautiful Spanish woman. &quot;Mom&quot; died, and Lola knows her only from her father, Archibald. Archie married against his family's wishes, and they are apparently a family of powerful Mages. In my Mage, there are a few important families of Mages, so this isn't a problem.<br /> <br /> Lola was Created by Archie, but she doesn't know this, and the player has not decided how. I'm thinking making a new person is, at a minimum, Life 5, Spirit 5, Mind 5. Here are my ideas for possible directions. I'd like help both considering these ideas, and any other devious plots that come to mind. Some of this is pretty dark, but hey, they don't call it WoD for nothing.<br /> <br /> 1. Lola was an unborn child, and Archibald used his magick to keep her alive after his wife died. He was overwhelmed with grief, and decided to &quot;improve&quot; upon her.<br /> 2. Archie and the wife wanted kids, but she died before that could happen. Being &quot;only&quot; a Master of two Spheres rather than three, he was forced to cut some corners to fulfill his wife's final wish.<br /> 2A: Not a Master of Spirit, he &quot;dumped&quot; his wife's soul into his daughter.<br /> 2B: Lola is essentially a clone of her &quot;mother&quot;, made mostly with Life.<br /> 2C: Lola is a XX clone of Archie, and was then imbued with his wife's memories.<br /> 3. Archie's little escapade pissed off his family, and they want control of Lola to keep her from embarrassing them and harming their political fortunes.<br /> 4. Archie's &quot;wife&quot; was a figment of a particularly deep Quiet, and he created Lola in that image.<br /> 5. Archie didn't create Lola alone. He and his wife were part of a cabal of Mages trying to make a person, and he stole the result. The wife was either in on the theft and got killed, or turned on him when he made a break for it.<br /> 6. Lola's Mom isn't dead; she went Marauder/Nephandi/is stuck in Quiet.<br /> <br /> Any other thoughts on where to take this?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}